Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"YBFuCp16mq4Q4UF7Zfg2Vw","review_id":"ayIMh6NpwlA8wqZw1jVWwQ","date":"2021-07-24T04:11:43","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9711570739746094,"text_excerpt":"Ooh Barracuda! When I first heard that Algiers point was getting a Barracuda Taco stand, I was pretty excited. Barracuda is one of the more popular taco places in New Orleans. This location is an old Gulf station, which is an icon of the neighborhood. David and I stopped in to see what it was all about. First of all, all of the seating is outside, so if you have an issue with the heat, you might want to get your tacos and margaritas to go. I got a couple of pork tacos, and David got the chicken taco. The pork taco was excellent. It was a bit spicy, with big chunks of spicy, juicy pork. It was a bit messy, but I really enjoyed it. I didn't get to try any of the Margaritas this time, but th..."},{"business_id":"YBFuCp16mq4Q4UF7Zfg2Vw","review_id":"Du6qBoJcwi-gWmNC2i57Vw","date":"2021-07-22T19:39:01","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9711569547653198,"text_excerpt":"Its been a long time coming. Located in an old 76 station, Barracuda has planted roots on Algiers point. Come to me Baby. All the usuals served up in a darling little outdoor dining area. Cleverly designed this surely will become a destination when visiting Algiers Point. Ride the ferry over and order up a margarita. Today i ordered the pollo bowl, a mexican coke and a margarita....Bill had tacos, but gobbled them up real quick(hence no photo) simply deliciousness was had... I feel a healthy habit starting. Welcome Barracuda!"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"YBFuCp16mq4Q4UF7Zfg2Vw","photo_id":"QjNvTjCrwVAh8eet9C_Mpg","label":"outside","image_url":